// dsl/extdeps/cron/mock_corpus.dag
// Scope: the cron layer's PUBLISHED mock corpus as a closed, declared structural fact.
// Anchor: DESIGN.md §3 (single authority) / §6 (model-just-in-time, mark the carrier).
//
// SINGLE authority for WHICH cron.Tab operations are hermetically realizable. Read by BOTH the
// compile-time M2 mock_totality_lens (src/v2/lens/mock_totality.dag, via the per-layer witness)
// AND the v1 runtime's eval_service_call (the M4 hermetic-realization fold) — one model, not two.
// The v1 runtime loads the dsl/ tree, so this corpus lives in dsl/ for the runtime to reach the
// SAME model the lens reads. Modeled on the M4.0 filesystem pilot
// (dsl/extdeps/filesystem/mock_corpus.dag, #5188).
//
// Rows inhabit std.hermetic_replay.PublishedMockCase. The operation set authority remains
// dsl/extdeps/cron/cron.dag (`service cron.Tab`); per-case payloads live in the Phase-2
// RecordedFixture store ONLY — rows carry the (operation_key, case_id) structural key.

module extdeps.cron.mock_corpus

import std.hermetic_replay { PublishedMockCase }

data cron_tab_mock_case_list: PublishedMockCase = PublishedMockCase {
  operation_key: "cron.Tab.List",
  service: "cron.Tab",
  operation: "List",
  case_id: 0
}

data cron_tab_mock_case_replace: PublishedMockCase = PublishedMockCase {
  operation_key: "cron.Tab.Replace",
  service: "cron.Tab",
  operation: "Replace",
  case_id: 0
}

// 🟡 gated — feature:cron-mock-corpus-from-service-decl — bind node://adhoc-aeaa1c56-be5
// dissolve-on-arrival: project this corpus directly from the `service cron.Tab` operation set in
// dsl/extdeps/cron/cron.dag (the SINGLE authority for WHICH operations exist), joined with the
// Phase-2 RecordedFixture store (the authority for WHICH recorded cases exist per operation), once
// a v2 lens can read a service decl's operation nodes and the fixture store's keys; this declared
// list then deletes in the same PR. forbidden: a row carrying a response VALUE (entries/success/
// stdout/stderr) — that would fork the payload authority, now owned by the fixture store (§3);
// rows mirror the (operation_key, case_id) structural key ONLY, and grow when a published
// operation/case is added upstream.
data cron_published_mock_corpus: List<PublishedMockCase> = [
  cron_tab_mock_case_list,
  cron_tab_mock_case_replace
]
